    <item>
      <title>MySQL DISTINCT Clause - VS Code</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/mysql/mysql-distinct-vs-code/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 15 Sep 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/mysql/mysql-distinct-vs-code/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;introduction-to-mysql-distinct-clause&#34;&gt;Introduction to MySQL DISTINCT Clause&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When querying data from a table, duplicate rows may be retrieved. To remove these duplicates, the DISTINCT clause is used in the SELECT statement. The syntax for the DISTINCT clause is as follows:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sql&#34; data-lang=&#34;sql&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;SELECT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;DISTINCT&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    select_list&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;FROM&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;table_name&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;WHERE&lt;/span&gt; &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    search_condition&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;ORDER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;BY&lt;/span&gt; &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    sort_expression;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;In this syntax, you specify one or more columns in the &lt;code&gt;select_list&lt;/code&gt; to obtain distinct values. If one column is specified, uniqueness is evaluated based on its values. If multiple columns are specified, uniqueness is determined by the combination of values in those columns.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
